{
  "dom_id": "step-q101642",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Solve for $t$ where $3(2t-1)=\\frac{4t-3}{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(2t-1) & =\\frac{4t-3}{2} \\\\ 2\\cdot (3(2t-1)) & =2(\\frac{4t-3}{2}) \\\\ 6(2t-1) & =\\cancel{2}(\\frac{4t-3}{\\cancel{2}}) \\\\ 12t-6 & =4t-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12t-6 & =4t-3 \\\\ 12t-6-4t & =-3+4t-4t \\\\ 8t-6 & =-3 \\\\ 8t-6+6 & =-3+6 \\\\ 8t & =3 \\\\ \\frac{8t}{8} & =\\frac{3}{8} \\\\ t & =\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
